Sporting a unique metallic teal-green and silver armor finish, "Piston" shares the aggressive, angular plate structure of Mark XXX ("Blue Steel") and Mark XXXIII ("Silver Centurion"). Tony optimized the thrusters in its boots and back flight-pack to deliver bursts of rapid acceleration, allowing it to dart between targets at hyper-velocity speeds.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXXI answers the House Party Protocol call at the Norco oil rig, engaging multiple Extremis soldiers in high-speed aerial maneuvers before being torn apart by Extremis soldiers and ultimately destroyed in the "Clean Slate" protocol.
